Appendix G: Proofs of Key Propositions

G.1 Proof of Proposition A.1 (Monotonicity)

The CES aggregator is:

g(Q, H, M) = \left[ \alpha (qQ)^\rho + (1-\alpha) H^\rho \right]^{1/\rho} \cdot \phi(M)

For \rho < 1, the derivative with respect to Q is:

g_Q = \phi(M) \cdot \frac{1}{\rho} \left[ \alpha (qQ)^\rho + (1-\alpha) H^\rho \right]^{1/\rho - 1} \cdot \alpha \rho (qQ)^{\rho-1} \cdot q

Simplifying:

g_Q = \phi(M) \cdot \alpha q (qQ)^{\rho-1} \left[ \alpha (qQ)^\rho + (1-\alpha) H^\rho \right]^{1/\rho - 1}

Since \phi(M) > 0, \alpha > 0, q > 0, (qQ)^{\rho-1} > 0, and the bracket is positive, g_Q > 0. Similarly for g_H. \square

G.2 Proof of Proposition A.2 (Concavity)

The CES function is concave for \rho \leq 1. The Hessian is negative semi-definite. The Cobb-Douglas multiplier \phi(M) is positive and independent of (Q,H), so it preserves concavity. \square

G.3 Proof of the First-Order Condition

The social planner's problem is:

\max_{Q_d} \int_\Theta R \cdot g(Q_d + Q^0, H, M) dF(\theta) - (p_q + e) \int_\Theta Q_d dF(\theta) - K(Q_d)

The first-order condition is:

\int_\Theta R \cdot g_Q(Q_d^* + Q^0, H, M) dF(\theta) - (p_q + e) \int_\Theta dF(\theta) - K'(Q_d^*) = 0

Since \int_\Theta dF(\theta) = 1:

\int_\Theta R \cdot g_Q(Q_d^* + Q^0, H, M) dF(\theta) = p_q + e + K'(Q_d^*)

This is the condition stated in Section 5.3. \square

G.4 Proof of the Stability Condition

The dynamic reinvestment loop is:

R_{CCD,t} = \tau_{\text{contractual}} R_{\text{commercial}}(Q_{c,t})

Q_{d,t+1} = s \cdot R_{CCD,t}

Q_{c,t+1} = Q_{c,t} + \Delta Q_c(Q_{d,t})

Linearizing around the steady state:

\begin{pmatrix} Q_{d,t+1} \\ Q_{c,t+1} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & s \tau \frac{\partial R_{\text{commercial}}}{\partial Q_c} \\ \frac{\partial \Delta Q_c}{\partial Q_d} & 1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} Q_{d,t} \\ Q_{c,t} \end{pmatrix}

The stability condition requires the spectral radius of the Jacobian to be less than 1:

\left| s \tau \frac{\partial R_{\text{commercial}}}{\partial Q_c} \right| < 1

This is the condition stated in Section 10, Stage 5. \square

