Concentration test HHI increase > 10% Reject if market concentration increases

H.2 Multiple Hypothesis Correction

For k = 6 tests, the Bonferroni-corrected significance level is \alpha_{\text{Bonf}} = 0.05/6 = 0.0083. Alternatively, use the Benjamini-Hochberg procedure to control the false discovery rate at 5%.

H.3 Power Analysis for the \gamma Test

Using the Toner-Rodgers effect size (now retracted) as an upper bound and the OECD SME survey as a lower bound, assume a 10% increase in patenting with \sigma = 0.5. For 80% power at 5% significance:

N = \frac{2 \cdot (1.96 + 0.84)^2 \cdot 0.25}{0.01} = 392

For a 5% effect:

N = \frac{2 \cdot 7.84 \cdot 0.25}{0.0025} = 1,568

The proposed N = 2,000 is sufficient for both.

